 "triggers": true,
 "note": "Gmail's trigger pass, TG0 to TG8 of docs/I07-BUILD-MAP.md section 8, on the test account, on the certification Fabric, run with --triggers --leave. What it sends stays in the mailbox, marked synthetic. One mailbox tells several watches of one mail, so each test polls every watch a write reaches, or its counts would carry to the next test. TG4, TG6 and TG8 are your hand steps, together. Each mail you send by hand takes a Find emails after it arrives and before the next poll: a proxied read gives the guard bytes, so only an action's search lists a mail, and a read the guard refuses skips that item for good. TG1's saved history answers probes U1 and U3, TGO's U6, TG4 and TG6 U4, and TG5 U8. TG7 needs probe U7's answer. If neither 1 nor an id above current answered 404, keep this run's first historyId and run TG7 alone after 8 days.",
